===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|すな|yomi=k|alt=沙}}

Attested in the ''{{w|Myōgoki}}'' (1275). According to one theory,<ref name="NKD2P"/> the word is shortened from earlier attested {{m|ja|砂子|tr=sunago|t=sand}}; see there for more.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|すな|acc=0|acc_ref=NKD2P,DJR,NHK,ZAJ}}
{{ja-accent-dialectal|region=Kyoto|k-0|すな|súná|ref=<ref name="NKD2P"/><ref name="ZAJ"/>}}
{{ja-accent-dialectal|region=Kagoshima|kt-a||す|な|súnà|ref=<ref name="ZAJ"/>}}
Some dialects in the Shikoku and Kyūshū regions have the initial consonant irregularly voiced in the standalone noun, as ''zuna''. This includes the dialects of {{w|Ehime dialect|Shūsō}}, {{w|Iyo dialect|Iyo}}, {{w|Kochi dialect|Tosa}}, {{w|Nagasaki dialect|Nagasaki}}, {{w|Tsushima dialect|Tsushima}}, {{w|Shimabara dialect|Shimabara}}, {{w|Saga dialect|Saga}}, {{w|Kagoshima dialect|Kagoshima}}, and {{w|Ōsumi dialect|Ōsumi}}.<ref name="NKD2P"/><ref name="GNHD">{{R:Hirayama et al 1992-1994|volume=3|pages=2623-2625}}</ref>

====Noun====
